{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 9, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "## Lost (and Found!) in Japan\n\nJust back from the most incredible trip to Japan! It was a whirlwind of ancient temples, neon lights, and delicious food. I spent a week exploring Tokyo, Kyoto, and a little bit of Hakone.\n\nTokyo was a sensory overload in the best way. Shibuya Crossing is truly a sight to behold – a perfectly orchestrated chaos of people! I loved exploring the quirky shops in Harajuku and the serene Meiji Jingu Shrine. The food scene is unbelievable; from ramen to sushi to takoyaki, I ate my way through the city.\n\nKyoto felt like stepping back in time. The temples and gardens were breathtaking, especially Fushimi Inari Shrine with its thousands of vibrant red torii gates winding up the mountain. I wandered through Gion, hoping to catch a glimpse of a geisha, and learned about traditional tea ceremonies.\n\nHakone offered stunning views of Mount Fuji and relaxing onsen (hot springs). Soaking in the mineral-rich water with that view was pure bliss.\n\nNavigating the train system was surprisingly easy, and everyone was so incredibly polite and helpful. I definitely learned a few Japanese phrases (arigato goes a long way!). \n\nJapan is a country of contrasts – modern and traditional, bustling and peaceful. It's a place that truly captivates the soul. I can't wait to go back!\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "##", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": "▁Lost", "logprob": -0.0011177966371178627}, {"token": "▁(", "logprob": -0.18502815067768097}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": "▁Found", "logprob": -0.0015026956098154187}, {"token": "!)", "logprob": -2.017681121826172}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁Japan", "logprob": -0.011610083281993866}, {"token": "\n\n", "logprob": -0.0008226824575103819}, {"token": "Just", "logprob": -0.49851635098457336}, {"token": "▁back", "logprob": -0.074449785